An opt-in `--verification-module-window K` option of `dafny verify` keeps up to K modules in verification at once, instead of finishing each module before translating and starting the next. Results, diagnostics, progress, logs and the exit code are reported in the same order as with the default K = 1, each proof sends the solver the same commands, and `--verification-module-window-memory` bounds the managed heap at which another module is admitted.
